WEBVTT

1
00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:45.461
- Ally, recap?
- Remember the Kowolskis?

2
00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:46.879
They've owned this shop
for 30 years, and they are
attempting to set a record

3
00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:50.716
by making
Buffalo's largest cookie,
and you have to wear this.

4
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.468
- A hair net?
- Health department.

5
00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:54.219
You're kidding me.
If you're working
around the cookie,

6
00:00:54.304 --> 00:00:55.304
you have to have it on.

7
00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:59.016
It's the law.
I just did the hair.
The hair is perfect.

8
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.559
All right. Give it to me.

9
00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.899
God, why do you hate me?

10
00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:09.443
We're rolling. And speed.

11
00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:12.654
For three decades,
the Kowolski family bakery

12
00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.491
has been a mainstay
in downtown Buffalo,

13
00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:19.578
known for their
sinfully sweet,
cream-filled Polski Pierogis,

14
00:01:19.662 --> 00:01:23.457
and the occasional
sugar-induced coma
that follows.

15
00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:26.418
But today, in honor of
their 30th anniversary,

16
00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:30.923
they've invited us
to ride along
as they go for the record

17
00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:33.592
on Buffalo's biggest cookie.

18
00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:40.015
Vol. Vol.
You need a tissue
or something?

19
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.726
Can we get Vol a tissue
or a spoon?

20
00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:44.561
It's a good thing
we're wearing these today,

21
00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:46.146
'cause I wouldn't want
any stray hairs

22
00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:48.148
to fall into the booger.

23
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:51.026
Are we gonna do this again?
No. We can cut to B-roll.

24
00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:57.199
Moving on! So tell me, Mama.
Why make
Buffalo's biggest cookie?

25
00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:00.494
Well, man
from health department

26
00:02:00.578 --> 00:02:06.041
say he find
rat pellet in our pastry,
but I say, "No."

27
00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:11.839
ls big chocolate sprinkle.
But he shut store down.

28
00:02:11.923 --> 00:02:16.051
So we clean up,
make big cookie

29
00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:19.888
for to bring customers back.

30
00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:24.017
Well, I admire your candor.
Let's try that again,
shall we?

31
00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:28.897
So tell me, Mama.
Why make
Buffalo's biggest cookie?

32
00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:33.318
So the children
of the neighborhood
will be happy?

33
00:02:33.403 --> 00:02:38.282
That's right. it must be
wonderful seeing the smiles
on their little faces.

34
00:02:38.366 --> 00:02:40.826
I work in back.
I see no smiles.

35
00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:46.790
The previous Buffalo record
was eight feet, seven inches,

36
00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:48.333
baked by Gladys Pelsnick.

37
00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:51.503
If this cookie beats Gladys's,
it will prove once and for all

38
00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:53.964
that the Kowolskis
have much more free time.

39
00:02:54.048 --> 00:02:57.676
And the cookie is 10 feet,
four inches.

40
00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.679
We have a new record!

41
00:03:00.763 --> 00:03:04.224
Cue the cheesy
inspirational music!

42
00:03:21.492 --> 00:03:24.161
But what are we
really looking at here?

43
00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:29.208
Is it just a big cookie,
or does this cookie represent
the pride of Buffalo,

44
00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:33.045
its dedicated
and hardworking citizens
the key ingredient,

45
00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:35.881
with a few nuts thrown in,

46
00:03:35.965 --> 00:03:40.802
and, finally, the love of
our families, which provides
the warm, chewy center,

47
00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:45.307
making our beloved Buffalo
the sweetest place to live.

48
00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.268
And that's the way
the cookie crumbles.

49
00:03:48.353 --> 00:03:53.315
I'm Bruce Nolan,
Eyewitness News.
And cut it.

50
00:03:55.318 --> 00:03:57.236
What do you think?

51
00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.780
I think it's really good.
It sucks.

52
00:03:59.864 --> 00:04:01.615
It's a story about a cookie.

53
00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:04.409
The Pillsbury Doughboy
will be riveted.

54
00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:07.412
Honey, it was funny.
It made me laugh.

55
00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:09.414
There's nothing wrong
with making people laugh.

56
00:04:09.499 --> 00:04:11.667
I'll never be an anchorman,
not with this.

57
00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.418
The job's right there,
but I can't reach it,

58
00:04:13.503 --> 00:04:15.545
because every time
they make me do this stuff,

59
00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.507
I have to act
like a total goof
in order to make it work.

60
00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:22.052
I have no credibility.
Not good. Not good.

61
00:04:22.136 --> 00:04:23.553
You know what?
Now you're just
sounding silly.

62
00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:24.638
Know what? Forget it.

63
00:04:24.722 --> 00:04:27.266
It's not important, right?
It's not important.

64
00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.142
Let's watch it one more time.
Oh, no.

65
00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:31.353
Just once more. Please?
No. No.

66
00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:35.023
Bruce, you promised
you would help
with this album.

67
00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.484
Now, you get
your goofy butt over here.

68
00:04:39.362 --> 00:04:40.362
Uh-uh.

69
00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.031
Okay.

70
00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:48.036
Okay. Okay. Now, you just
go through this stack,

71
00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.205
and you pick
your favorites.

72
00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:57.462
Oh, come on.
This is fun. Right?
Isn't this fun?

73
00:04:57.547 --> 00:04:58.880
This is nice.

74
00:04:59.882 --> 00:05:01.800
Evan's gonna get
that anchor job,
I just know it.

75
00:05:01.884 --> 00:05:03.510
Ah, Bruce!
He's the favorite.

76
00:05:03.594 --> 00:05:06.013
All right. You know what?
Just forget it.
Let's just forget it.

77
00:05:06.097 --> 00:05:10.475
This is just our life.
We can always just have
some kid do it for us.

78
00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:16.148
Whoa! Hold the phone!
I like this one.
Our weekend at the lake.

79
00:05:16.232 --> 00:05:18.775
How did you get that?
That's supposed to be
in our private stash.

80
00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:21.987
You look perky, hon.
It must've been cold.
All right. Just give it to me.

81
00:05:22.071 --> 00:05:23.405
I think I'll put this
on my computer

82
00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:24.781
and use it as wallpaper.
No, no, no.

83
00:05:24.866 --> 00:05:26.992
Okay. Give it to me. Come on!
No, no, no.

84
00:05:27.076 --> 00:05:31.079
All right. Fine.
Do with it what you will.
I don't care.

85
00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:33.790
I will do with it
what I will.
Jesus.

86
00:05:35.752 --> 00:05:38.253
You know, I might even
send this in to Playboy.

87
00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:42.132
I hear their layouts
can be quite tasteful.
Give that to me right now!

88
00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:43.300
Jesus.
Right now!

89
00:05:43.384 --> 00:05:45.677
Rough stuff!
I'm gonna hurt you...

90
00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.018
Sweetie? Time to get up.

91
00:05:55.772 --> 00:05:58.482
Good dream. No. No.

92
00:06:07.617 --> 00:06:11.995
Well, the Buffalo Sabres lost
again last night at the hands
of the Toronto Maple Leafs.

93
00:06:12.121 --> 00:06:15.165
It was a shootout
on the ice for our home...
Of course. They're my team.

94
00:06:15.249 --> 00:06:17.417
And that's the way
the cookie crumbles.

95
00:06:17.502 --> 00:06:20.379
You know, I think
there might be something
to this cookie line.

96
00:06:20.463 --> 00:06:23.590
All the greatest anchors
have had their own
signature sign-off,

97
00:06:23.674 --> 00:06:26.218
like Wal-ter Cron-kite.

98
00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:33.433
And that's the way it was.
That's the way
the cookie crumbles.

99
00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:37.312
And that's the way...
l like it...

100
00:06:39.774 --> 00:06:42.234
Oh, no. Grace, the dog!

101
00:06:42.318 --> 00:06:43.944
I'm in the shower!

102
00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.409
No, Sam! Bad dog!

103
00:06:50.493 --> 00:06:55.038
Inside, bad. Outside, good.

104
00:06:59.502 --> 00:07:02.337
Oh, you're done now. Great.

105
00:07:03.047 --> 00:07:06.133
B-E-A-utiful.

106
00:07:07.552 --> 00:07:10.429
Come on.
Let's go back inside
and have a shit.

107
00:07:15.852 --> 00:07:19.354
What is the deal-io?
We are having a blood drive.

108
00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.481
Creepy. Needles. Yuck.

109
00:07:21.566 --> 00:07:24.526
Well, they need my blood.
I have a very rare blood type.

110
00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.945
I'm A. B. -positive.
Really?

111
00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:28.363
I'm I. B. -positive.

112
00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:32.617
I be positive,
they ain't touching me with
no needle. it's just so...

113
00:07:32.702 --> 00:07:36.246
Helpful and lifesaving?
No. it's your blood.
It's blood.

114
00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:39.207
Blood's supposed to
stay inside the body.
That's where it's meant to be.

115
00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:41.877
Besides, they stockpile
this stuff
in a warehouse somewhere.

116
00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:44.713
It's all frozen on ice,
and they tell everybody
there's a shortage.

117
00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.174
That's just not true.
Where did you hear that?

118
00:07:47.258 --> 00:07:49.759
From a very reliable
friend of a friend of a girl,

119
00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:52.846
whose sister's going out
with someone very high up
in the government.

120
00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:55.307
But for your own protection,
I cannot discuss it
at this time.

121
00:07:55.391 --> 00:07:57.017
Now, get out
before they see us together.

122
00:07:57.101 --> 00:07:58.310
Oh, no.

123
00:08:01.397 --> 00:08:04.858
Oh. Here. Hold on a second.
You need these more than I do.

124
00:08:04.942 --> 00:08:07.235
What is these?
Prayer beads.

125
00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:11.239
The kids made them for me.
They will keep you safe.

126
00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:12.657
I hope they're powerful.

127
00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:16.244
I'm gonna need
a frigging miracle
to get to work on time.

128
00:08:26.797 --> 00:08:30.759
This isn't happening.
Not now.
Not during sweeps week.

129
00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:33.678
Not during sweeps week!

130
00:08:34.931 --> 00:08:36.598
Oh, God.

131
00:08:37.475 --> 00:08:40.268
Yeah. Yeah.
Meeting's started without me.

132
00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:43.396
This is my luck.
This is my luck!

133
00:08:45.733 --> 00:08:47.234
Shit.

134
00:08:49.403 --> 00:08:51.863
Oh, come on. Come on.
Come on. Come on!

135
00:08:55.326 --> 00:08:59.454
Jesus. Get out of there!

136
00:09:03.918 --> 00:09:07.462
"R Ewe Blind."
No, but I'm late.

137
00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:12.217
Is your child
in dire jeopardy?

138
00:09:12.301 --> 00:09:14.052
Find out tonight
after the game.

139
00:09:14.136 --> 00:09:15.595
Okay. Promos are approved.

140
00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.180
Now, let's...
Uh, Jack,

141
00:09:17.265 --> 00:09:19.516
shouldn't we be focusing
on Pete's retirement?

142
00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:20.767
I mean, this is his last week.

143
00:09:20.851 --> 00:09:23.311
Yeah, Jack. Any word on
the open anchor position?

144
00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:26.439
Evan, when I know something,
you'll know something.

145
00:09:27.149 --> 00:09:30.193
Sorry I'm late. Traffic was...

146
00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:34.114
Did you guys
already play the spots?
It's a nice story, Bruce,

147
00:09:34.198 --> 00:09:36.074
but we're gonna go
with Evan's piece,

148
00:09:36.158 --> 00:09:39.369
sex scandal
in the mayor's office
for sweeps.

149
00:09:39.453 --> 00:09:42.664
Oh, yeah. Sweeps.

150
00:09:44.125 --> 00:09:46.960
And that's the way
the cookie crumbles.

151
00:09:48.296 --> 00:09:50.255
I'm just
messing with you, Bruce.

152
00:09:50.339 --> 00:09:56.761
See, you just got to
remember that the newsroom
is like a big cookie.

153
00:09:58.514 --> 00:10:00.640
Do you like jazz, Evan?
Yeah.

154
00:10:00.725 --> 00:10:02.350
Let me play something for you.

155
00:10:09.525 --> 00:10:12.611
I can hold that note
all day, buddy.
Knock it off, guys.

156
00:10:12.695 --> 00:10:14.863
Bruce, we're gonna
keep your story in reserve.

157
00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:16.364
Now, can we get back
to the board,

158
00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:19.159
so we'll have something
to put on the air today?

159
00:10:19.452 --> 00:10:22.537
Great choice, Jack.
This is the Cadillac
of bolognas.

160
00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:25.165
Okay. Thanks.
Jack, can I talk
to you a second?

161
00:10:25.249 --> 00:10:27.792
Yeah. Sure, Bruce.
What do you need?
Sweeps.

162
00:10:27.877 --> 00:10:30.462
Bruce.
Jack. Jack!
Hear me out here.

163
00:10:30.546 --> 00:10:31.921
I'm starting
to get desperate, man.

164
00:10:32.006 --> 00:10:34.382
I'm pushing 40,
and what have I got
to show for it?

165
00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:36.134
I've hit some kind
of a ceiling here.

166
00:10:36.218 --> 00:10:38.803
There's an anti-Bruce barrier
I can't get past.

167
00:10:38.888 --> 00:10:42.182
And Evan is loving it,
by the way. Loving it.

168
00:10:42.266 --> 00:10:46.186
He gets the stories.
He gets on sweeps. Maybe
I should be more like Evan.

169
00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:48.730
You don't wanna be like Evan.
Evan's an asshole.

170
00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:51.650
I can be an asshole.
No, Bruce. You can't.

171
00:10:56.572 --> 00:10:59.407
You gonna pick that up?
Yeah. I'm sorry.
It's... I'm losing it.

172
00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:02.994
It's just this
whole anchor thing opening up
has got me nuts.

173
00:11:03.079 --> 00:11:04.079
Hi, Susan.

174
00:11:04.163 --> 00:11:05.955
Hi, Susan.
Hi, Jack.

175
00:11:07.541 --> 00:11:10.669
Look, Bruce.
You're a good reporter.
You make people laugh.

176
00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:17.801
All right. I'll tell you what.
Today is the 156th anniversary
of the Maid of the Mist.

177
00:11:17.885 --> 00:11:19.886
I want you at Niagara Falls
in an hour.

178
00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.681
Maid of the Mist?
That's always live.

179
00:11:23.766 --> 00:11:25.350
But Evan
always does live feeds.

180
00:11:25.434 --> 00:11:28.228
Now you and Evan
get the live feeds.

181
00:11:28.312 --> 00:11:31.731
I'm going live? During sweeps?
But watch your step, Bruce.

182
00:11:31.857 --> 00:11:36.027
I've seen your outtakes.
Jack, you will
not regret this.

183
00:11:36.112 --> 00:11:39.823
And I won't forget you
when I go national.
Uh, can you...

184
00:11:41.283 --> 00:11:42.742
Thanks, pal.

185
00:11:43.828 --> 00:11:47.580
Can I have your wish now?
I'm gonna put it in
the wish jar. Thank you.

186
00:11:47.665 --> 00:11:49.874
Okay. Put your wish in there.
Me too.

187
00:11:49.959 --> 00:11:53.795
Put your wish in there.
Look at that.
Looks like a big wish.

188
00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:57.006
Oh, no, no. Oh, no. Martin,
don't... Don't eat that.
Don't eat that.

189
00:11:57.091 --> 00:12:00.176
Don't put that in your mouth.
That's paste, honey.

190
00:12:01.971 --> 00:12:05.724
That must've tasted awful.
Mommy!

191
00:12:05.808 --> 00:12:09.728
Oh, Zoe-Baboey!
Did you have a good time
with Aunt Crazy today?

192
00:12:09.812 --> 00:12:13.398
Yeah? See how nice this is?
Baby on the hip?

193
00:12:13.482 --> 00:12:15.275
Oh, it's amazing.
You've become Mom.

194
00:12:15.359 --> 00:12:17.902
The transformation
is complete.

195
00:12:19.029 --> 00:12:20.447
Oh.
I'll get it.

196
00:12:20.531 --> 00:12:22.240
- Small Wonders Day Care.
- Grace?

197
00:12:22.324 --> 00:12:24.826
No. it's Debbie,
the sister whose life
you're not wasting.

198
00:12:24.952 --> 00:12:27.912
Oh, all right.
Okay, okay, okay.
Bye, Debbie!

199
00:12:27.997 --> 00:12:32.917
Hi. Hi. Sorry. Debbie forgot
to take her meds today.
Where are you?

200
00:12:33.002 --> 00:12:38.006
Oh, a little place called
the winner's circle. I'm at
the falls doing a live report.

201
00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:41.259
Live? That's great!
Yeah! it's happening, hon.

202
00:12:41.343 --> 00:12:43.052
I got sweeps, and I'm live.

203
00:12:43.137 --> 00:12:45.638
You know what that means?
They're seeing
if I can think on my feet,

204
00:12:45.723 --> 00:12:48.558
you know, like, I might
have to do in a live news
anchor situation.

205
00:12:48.642 --> 00:12:50.185
Oh, my gosh.

206
00:12:50.269 --> 00:12:52.687
Yeah.
It's what we've always
talked about, Grace.

207
00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:55.607
Jack practically came out
and told me.
Practically?

208
00:12:55.691 --> 00:12:58.401
Well, he didn't spell it out,
but legally, he can't.

209
00:12:58.486 --> 00:13:00.278
But this is exactly
what happened to Susan Ortega

210
00:13:00.362 --> 00:13:03.072
just before
they bumped her up.

211
00:13:03.157 --> 00:13:05.241
It's good. it's good.
It's good.

212
00:13:05.326 --> 00:13:07.452
Okay. Well, honey,
I just don't...

213
00:13:07.536 --> 00:13:09.662
I don't want you
to get too ahead of yourself.

214
00:13:09.789 --> 00:13:12.123
Bruce?
Oh, I got to go.
They're calling me in.

215
00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:14.292
Oh. Okay, honey.
Good luck. I love you.

216
00:13:14.376 --> 00:13:16.377
Love, love, love,
love, love.

217
00:13:17.087 --> 00:13:18.671
Let's do it.

218
00:13:18.756 --> 00:13:21.925
They want you
close to the falls.
Really?

219
00:13:22.009 --> 00:13:23.802
I'm gonna get soaked.
That's the point.

220
00:13:23.886 --> 00:13:25.470
They want you to put this on.

221
00:13:25.554 --> 00:13:28.389
Part of the condition of us
getting the exclusive.

222
00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:32.477
You know what?
Nothing can bother me today.
Nothing.

223
00:13:32.561 --> 00:13:36.523
Okay. Now, remember.
It's their
156th-year anniversary.

224
00:13:36.607 --> 00:13:38.650
149 capacity.
Right.

225
00:13:38.776 --> 00:13:42.362
They cater to tourists,
honeymooners...
And people insanely thirsty.

226
00:13:42.446 --> 00:13:43.488
I get it.
Okay.

227
00:13:43.572 --> 00:13:46.324
And you are gonna
be interviewing
lrene Dansfield.

228
00:13:46.408 --> 00:13:49.285
Irene! Pleasure to meet you.
Truly.

229
00:13:49.411 --> 00:13:52.455
You look beautiful.
lrene's mother rode on
the maiden voyage.

230
00:13:52.581 --> 00:13:54.833
Wow. Rub that in my face,
why don't you?
Ninety seconds!

231
00:13:54.917 --> 00:13:58.753
Ninety seconds? Holy hell.
Uh, yeah. Okay. 90 seconds?

232
00:13:59.088 --> 00:14:04.217
Because of the fast response,
the toxic chemicals were
cleaned up without incident.

233
00:14:04.301 --> 00:14:07.345
Susan?
Bruce Nolan is standing by
at Niagara Falls,

234
00:14:07.429 --> 00:14:10.431
but before we go
live to Bruce, we have
an announcement to make.

235
00:14:10.933 --> 00:14:16.187
As everyone knows,
after 33 years, our beloved
Pete Fineman is retiring.

236
00:14:16.856 --> 00:14:21.609
Pete's shoes are
virtually impossible to fill,
but the show must go on,

237
00:14:21.694 --> 00:14:27.073
and we could think of
no one better than
our very own Evan Baxter.

238
00:14:27.491 --> 00:14:30.577
Oh... Oh, boy.

239
00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.872
Congratulations, Evan.
Thanks, Susan.
I'm thrilled and honored.

240
00:14:33.956 --> 00:14:34.956
And as you said,

241
00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:38.710
no one can replace
the great Pete Fineman,
but I will do my best.

242
00:14:38.794 --> 00:14:43.423
I have to say, I am so proud
to be a part of our
local community of Buffalo,

243
00:14:43.507 --> 00:14:48.595
and I think, in a lot of ways,
a great city is like
a great recipe, really.

244
00:14:48.679 --> 00:14:54.225
You take hardworking citizens,
add some caregivers,
maybe a few nuts,

245
00:14:57.479 --> 00:15:01.274
all sprinkled
with the love and support
of our good families.

246
00:15:01.358 --> 00:15:05.570
Ultimately, that makes
one sweet place to live.

247
00:15:05.654 --> 00:15:07.405
That was amazing.
I meant it.

248
00:15:07.489 --> 00:15:10.074
I wish I'd written something.
And now let's go live

249
00:15:10.159 --> 00:15:12.827
to that wacky Bruce Nolan
out at Niagara Falls.

250
00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:14.537
Hey! Wacky Bruce!

251
00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.877
Bruce? Talk, Bruce. Hello?

252
00:15:20.961 --> 00:15:22.962
Talk, honey. Talk.
What's going on?

253
00:15:23.047 --> 00:15:24.964
We got a Walt Disney.
He's frozen solid.

254
00:15:25.049 --> 00:15:26.758
We may not have audio.
Check the feed.

255
00:15:26.842 --> 00:15:29.177
We may be having a bit
of technical difficulty.

256
00:15:29.261 --> 00:15:30.261
Feed's good, Jack.

257
00:15:30.346 --> 00:15:33.306
Move. Come on. Come on.
Come on.
Talk, Bruce, damn it!

258
00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:36.142
All right. Get ready
to pull the plug.
Come on, baby.
Say something.

259
00:15:36.226 --> 00:15:39.687
Say something.
Bruce, talk.

260
00:15:42.733 --> 00:15:44.484
- Hi, Susan.
- Oh, thank you, God.

261
00:15:44.568 --> 00:15:46.861
Bruce Nolan here
aboard the Maid of the Mist

262
00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:49.530
in fabulous Niagara Falls,
New York.

263
00:15:50.074 --> 00:15:54.452
First off, let me just add
another congratulations
to Evan Backstabber...

264
00:15:54.536 --> 00:15:56.829
Pardon me. Bastard.
Baxter, rather.

265
00:15:56.914 --> 00:15:59.707
It is good to see
what someone
with talent can do,

266
00:15:59.792 --> 00:16:02.877
when great opportunities
are given to them
instead of me.

267
00:16:04.296 --> 00:16:08.383
Anyway, I'm here
with Katharine Hepburn's mom.
Tell me.

268
00:16:08.467 --> 00:16:10.718
Why did you throw the blue
Heart of the Ocean jewel

269
00:16:10.803 --> 00:16:13.012
over the railing
of the Titanic?

270
00:16:13.097 --> 00:16:15.390
Did you feel bad at all
letting Leo DiCaprio drown,

271
00:16:15.474 --> 00:16:18.101
while you were safe,
floating on the door?

272
00:16:18.185 --> 00:16:19.686
Could you have taken turns,

273
00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:23.189
or were you just too afraid
to freeze your big,
fat ass off?

274
00:16:24.233 --> 00:16:25.984
I guess that's how life is,
isn't it?

275
00:16:26.068 --> 00:16:30.863
Some people are drenched,
freezing to death on a stupid
boat, with a stupid hat,

276
00:16:30.948 --> 00:16:34.325
while others
are in a comfy news studio,
sucking up all the glory.

277
00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:37.829
- Oh, well. No big deal.
- Oh, boy.

278
00:16:37.913 --> 00:16:39.998
Oh, look.
It's the owner of
the Maid of the Mist.

279
00:16:40.082 --> 00:16:42.083
Let's have a talk with him,
shall we?
Come on in here, Bill.

280
00:16:42.167 --> 00:16:43.376
That's all right.
No, no, no, no. No, no.

281
00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:44.669
Come on. Let's have a talk.

282
00:16:44.753 --> 00:16:46.671
Come on. What are you doing?

283
00:16:46.755 --> 00:16:49.549
Bill, you've been running
the Maid of the Mist
for 23 years now.

284
00:16:49.633 --> 00:16:51.718
Tell me. Why do you think
I didn't get the anchor job?

285
00:16:51.844 --> 00:16:54.637
Hey, man.
I don't want problems.
Is it my hair, Bill?

286
00:16:54.722 --> 00:16:56.180
Are my teeth
not white enough?

287
00:16:56.265 --> 00:17:03.187
Or like the great falls,
is the bedrock of my life
eroding beneath me?

288
00:17:03.439 --> 00:17:08.776
Eroding! Eroding! Eroding!

289
00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:11.487
Cut the feed. Go to black.

290
00:17:11.572 --> 00:17:12.822
Go to black.
I'm on it.

291
00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:18.453
I'm Bruce Nolan
for Eyewitness News.
Back to you, fuckers!

292
00:17:19.872 --> 00:17:21.706
Oh, boy.
Oh, my God.

293
00:17:26.795 --> 00:17:31.632
That is perfect.
That is the motivation
that I needed!

294
00:17:31.717 --> 00:17:34.135
Right there! Thank you.

295
00:17:35.137 --> 00:17:38.264
Thank you, W. K. B. W.!

296
00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:42.143
Wimpy Kitty Baby Whiners!

297
00:17:42.227 --> 00:17:44.353
That's what that stands for!

298
00:17:45.773 --> 00:17:49.984
I'll see you on Channel 5,
where they do the real news.

299
00:17:51.278 --> 00:17:54.322
Do I look blind to you?
Do I look blind to you?

300
00:17:55.282 --> 00:17:58.910
Hey.
Let's go, man.
Come on. Let's go.

301
00:17:59.703 --> 00:18:04.290
What are you doing over there?
Come on.
Leave the poor guy alone.

302
00:18:05.125 --> 00:18:06.584
You okay, man?

303
00:18:08.545 --> 00:18:10.588
Yeah, you'd better
keep walking.

304
00:18:10.672 --> 00:18:12.757
What? What'd you say, ése?

305
00:18:12.841 --> 00:18:15.426
Run, man! Run!

306
00:18:17.054 --> 00:18:18.971
Oh, God!

307
00:18:21.225 --> 00:18:25.144
Okay, okay, okay!
I didn't mean it!
I was just kidding!

308
00:18:25.229 --> 00:18:27.188
Hey, you forgot your things.

309
00:18:31.777 --> 00:18:34.153
Say something to that.
Say something.

310
00:18:37.199 --> 00:18:43.454
B-E-A-utiful.

311
00:18:47.292 --> 00:18:49.919
That's what I get...

312
00:18:50.003 --> 00:18:53.297
That's what I get
for trying to help someone.

313
00:18:55.134 --> 00:18:57.677
Oh, don't look at me, Walter.

314
00:18:57.761 --> 00:18:59.512
Oh, no!

315
00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:08.855
Well, that's my payment,
I guess. That...
That is my reward.

316
00:19:13.735 --> 00:19:16.863
Just? Just get a clue!

317
00:19:18.198 --> 00:19:19.907
Thank God
you're all right.

318
00:19:19.992 --> 00:19:22.493
God. Yeah.
Let's thank God. Shall we?

319
00:19:22.578 --> 00:19:25.037
For his blessings
are raining down upon me.

320
00:19:25.164 --> 00:19:28.166
Wait! That's not rain!
Bruce, please
don't do that, honey.

321
00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.835
You know that
everything happens
for a reason.

322
00:19:30.919 --> 00:19:34.505
That I don't need.
That is a cliché.
That is not helpful to me.

323
00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:36.632
A bird in the hand
is worth two in the bush.

324
00:19:36.717 --> 00:19:40.011
I have no bird.
I have no bush. God has taken
my bird and my bush.

325
00:19:40.095 --> 00:19:43.306
Oh, I see.
So God is picking on you,
is that what you're saying?

326
00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:46.684
No. He's ignoring me
completely.

327
00:19:46.768 --> 00:19:50.188
He's far too busy
giving Evan
everything he wants.

328
00:19:50.272 --> 00:19:53.774
Oh, that's great, Sam,
but you missed your target.
I'm over here!

329
00:19:53.859 --> 00:19:56.235
Don't get mad at the dog.
It's not the dog's fault.

330
00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.988
No. it's God's fault.
I gave him
the wrong coordinates.

331
00:19:59.072 --> 00:20:00.406
All right. You know what?
Enough. All right?

332
00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:02.116
Will you stop being
such a martyr?

333
00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:04.785
I am not being a martyr.
I'm a victim.

334
00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.621
God is a mean kid
sitting on an anthill

335
00:20:06.705 --> 00:20:08.789
with a magnifying glass,
and I'm the ant.

336
00:20:08.874 --> 00:20:11.083
He could fix my life
in five minutes
if he wanted to,

337
00:20:11.168 --> 00:20:14.170
but he'd rather
burn off my feelers
and watch me squirm!

338
00:20:14.254 --> 00:20:17.048
Sweetheart,
I know you're mad.
It's understandable.

339
00:20:17.132 --> 00:20:22.887
What Evan did is slimy
and wrong, but this day
could've been so much worse.

340
00:20:22.971 --> 00:20:27.683
I'm just glad you're okay.
Okay? News flash!
I'm not okay.

341
00:20:27.768 --> 00:20:31.229
I'm not okay with
a mediocre job! I'm not okay
with a mediocre apartment.

342
00:20:31.313 --> 00:20:34.148
I'm not okay
with a mediocre life!

343
00:20:42.366 --> 00:20:45.826
So is that what you think
that we have?
A mediocre life?

344
00:20:45.911 --> 00:20:49.163
Don't make this about you.
About me?

345
00:20:49.248 --> 00:20:54.502
How could I make this
about me? it's about you!
It's always about you!

346
00:20:54.586 --> 00:20:57.213
Perfect. Perfect.

347
00:20:57.297 --> 00:20:59.257
I'll have
the worst day of my life

348
00:20:59.341 --> 00:21:01.926
with a side order of guilt,
please!

349
00:21:04.805 --> 00:21:05.846
Oh.

350
00:21:07.266 --> 00:21:11.102
Okay, God.
You want me to talk to you?

351
00:21:11.186 --> 00:21:14.397
Then talk back.
Tell me what's going on.

352
00:21:14.481 --> 00:21:17.358
What should I do?
Give me a signal.

353
00:21:19.278 --> 00:21:23.572
Oh, I need
your guidance, Lord.
Please send me a sign.

354
00:21:27.703 --> 00:21:30.121
Ah, what's this joker
doing now?

355
00:21:35.752 --> 00:21:39.255
Okay. All right.
I'll try it your way.

356
00:21:39.339 --> 00:21:44.427
All right.
Lord, I need a miracle.

357
00:21:45.554 --> 00:21:49.140
I'm desperate.
I need your help, Lord.

358
00:21:49.224 --> 00:21:53.144
Please reach into my life.
Hey!

359
00:21:54.563 --> 00:21:58.482
What the he...I got you!

360
00:22:24.801 --> 00:22:25.926
Hey!

361
00:22:42.444 --> 00:22:45.780
Fine! The gloves are off, pal!

362
00:22:45.864 --> 00:22:48.366
Come on!
Let me see a little wrath.

363
00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:52.119
Smite me, O mighty smiter!

364
00:22:53.205 --> 00:22:55.664
You're the one
who should be fired!

365
00:22:55.749 --> 00:23:00.419
The only one around here
not doing his job is you!

366
00:23:01.171 --> 00:23:03.631
Answer me!

367
00:23:18.397 --> 00:23:20.564
Sorry. Don't know you.

368
00:23:21.483 --> 00:23:23.567
Wouldn't call you if I did.

369
00:23:27.489 --> 00:23:28.739
Oh.

370
00:23:36.331 --> 00:23:38.833
Oh, God. Oh.

371
00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:47.341
Hello, "5550123."

372
00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:16.162
Oh, no! Sam,
this has got to stop.

373
00:24:18.748 --> 00:24:20.332
All right.
Now, get it straight here.

374
00:24:20.417 --> 00:24:23.461
That's the house.
This is the bathroom.
House. Bathroom.

375
00:24:23.545 --> 00:24:26.630
Bathroom. House.
House. Bathroom.
Bathroom. House.

376
00:24:29.050 --> 00:24:30.634
What's the point?

377
00:24:55.410 --> 00:24:58.245
"5550123"

378
00:25:00.624 --> 00:25:03.667
Denied that promotion at work?
Is life unfair?

379
00:25:03.752 --> 00:25:06.795
Is there someone
less talented than you
reaping all the benefits?

380
00:25:06.880 --> 00:25:10.966
Is your name Bruce?
Then do we have
the job for you.

381
00:25:11.051 --> 00:25:14.345
We're located at
7725623rd Street.

382
00:25:14.429 --> 00:25:18.015
So come on down,
or we'll just
keep beeping you.

383
00:25:35.075 --> 00:25:36.700
"Omni Presents."

384
00:25:37.911 --> 00:25:40.996
Oh, yeah.
The glass is half full.

385
00:25:41.456 --> 00:25:42.790
Oh, geez!

386
00:25:44.751 --> 00:25:50.005
Come on! Look!
What is that? What is that?

387
00:25:51.466 --> 00:25:54.802
Ah, geez! Thank you.
Thank you again.

388
00:26:02.644 --> 00:26:04.061
What the...

389
00:26:11.820 --> 00:26:13.821
You're looking for Room 7.

390
00:26:16.491 --> 00:26:18.409
Yeah. I figured.

391
00:26:18.493 --> 00:26:20.703
You want me
to even those up for you?

392
00:26:24.332 --> 00:26:25.916
How do I get to Room 7?

393
00:26:26.001 --> 00:26:29.587
That'll be on
the seventh floor.
Stairs are right over there.

394
00:26:29.671 --> 00:26:32.047
- I'd rather take the elevator.
- Out of order.

395
00:26:32.132 --> 00:26:35.259
I love the stairs though.
They were my second choice.

396
00:26:35.343 --> 00:26:37.761
Do you mind giving me a hand
with this floor?

397
00:26:37.846 --> 00:26:40.764
What? That's good.

398
00:26:42.058 --> 00:26:43.517
Are you serious?

399
00:26:43.602 --> 00:26:46.895
Oh, I'm kind of busy.

400
00:26:46.980 --> 00:26:51.025
Um, rain check.
I'll hold you to it.

401
00:26:52.277 --> 00:26:55.446
I'm free on the seventh
at 7:00.

402
00:26:58.158 --> 00:26:59.992
Seventh at 7:00 it is.

403
00:27:03.330 --> 00:27:05.122
This looks promising.

404
00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:17.176
Hello?
Another "hugantic, ginormic"
waste of my life.

405
00:27:17.886 --> 00:27:19.136
Hello?

406
00:27:20.972 --> 00:27:24.433
Yo! I'm looking
for whoever runs this joint.
Be right with you.

407
00:27:24.517 --> 00:27:28.145
I'm trying to fix a light.
Tell me if it's working.

408
00:27:28.229 --> 00:27:30.481
Yeah. Seems to be.

409
00:27:30.565 --> 00:27:34.443
Kind of bright, though.
Yeah. it is for most people.

410
00:27:34.527 --> 00:27:38.781
Spend their lives in the dark
trying to hide from me.

411
00:27:40.492 --> 00:27:42.660
Oh, the elevator's broken,
huh?

412
00:27:42.744 --> 00:27:45.663
Yeah,
but I'll get around to it.

413
00:27:47.123 --> 00:27:50.793
You install the Clapper?
No, but catchy jingle,
isn't it?

414
00:27:51.586 --> 00:27:56.090
Clap on, clap off.
Clap on, clap off the Clapper.

415
00:27:57.425 --> 00:27:59.593
Just can't
get it out of my head.

416
00:28:00.303 --> 00:28:03.847
Good luck with that.
I'm gonna go now.

417
00:28:03.932 --> 00:28:06.767
Okay. But the boss'll be
right out.

418
00:28:14.693 --> 00:28:19.071
You must be Bruce.
I've been expecting you.

419
00:28:21.491 --> 00:28:23.117
This is hilarious.

420
00:28:23.201 --> 00:28:25.953
So you're the boss
and the electrician
and the janitor?

421
00:28:26.037 --> 00:28:29.206
Must be
a killer Christmas party.
Don't get drunk, though.

422
00:28:29.290 --> 00:28:31.166
One of you might need
a ride home.

423
00:28:33.002 --> 00:28:37.256
You always were funny, Bruce,
just like your father.

424
00:28:37.340 --> 00:28:40.050
He didn't mind
rolling up his sleeves,
either, son.

425
00:28:40.135 --> 00:28:43.595
People underestimate
the benefit
of good old manual labor.

426
00:28:43.680 --> 00:28:46.724
There's freedom in it.
Some of the happiest people
in the world

427
00:28:46.808 --> 00:28:50.436
go home smelling
to high heaven
at the end of the day.

428
00:28:50.520 --> 00:28:52.563
All right. What is this?

429
00:28:52.647 --> 00:28:55.315
How do you know my father,
and how did you
get my pager number?

430
00:28:55.400 --> 00:28:58.110
Oh, I know quite a lot
about you, Bruce,

431
00:28:59.362 --> 00:29:01.989
just about everything
there is to know.

432
00:29:02.323 --> 00:29:07.035
Everything
you've ever said or done
or thought about doing,

433
00:29:08.288 --> 00:29:10.497
right there
in that file cabinet.

434
00:29:11.750 --> 00:29:15.127
Wow. A whole drawer
just for me.
Yeah.

435
00:29:15.211 --> 00:29:19.173
Mind if I take a look?
It's your life.

436
00:29:20.508 --> 00:29:22.342
This ought to be good.

437
00:29:37.025 --> 00:29:39.693
Now, this last entry
was a little disturbing.

438
00:29:51.456 --> 00:29:53.540
"The gloves are off, God.

439
00:29:53.666 --> 00:29:56.251
"God has taken my bird
and my bush.

440
00:29:56.336 --> 00:29:59.671
"God is a mean kid
with a magnifying glass."

441
00:29:59.756 --> 00:30:03.258
"Smite me, O mighty smiter!"

442
00:30:03.343 --> 00:30:07.554
Now, I'm not much
for blaspheming, but
that last one made me laugh.

443
00:30:07.639 --> 00:30:09.515
Are you spying on me?

444
00:30:13.061 --> 00:30:14.478
Who are you?

445
00:30:15.647 --> 00:30:17.231
I'm the one.

446
00:30:17.816 --> 00:30:21.485
Creator of the heavens
and the earth,
alpha and omega.

447
00:30:22.529 --> 00:30:24.822
Oh, I see where this is going.

448
00:30:24.906 --> 00:30:27.866
Bruce, I'm God.

449
00:30:27.951 --> 00:30:31.119
Bingo! Yahtzee!
Is that your final answer?

450
00:30:31.204 --> 00:30:35.833
Our survey says, "God!"
Bing, bing, bing, bing, bing!

451
00:30:35.917 --> 00:30:37.626
Well, it was
nice to meet you, God.

452
00:30:37.710 --> 00:30:39.086
Thank you
for the Grand Canyon,

453
00:30:39.170 --> 00:30:41.255
and good luck
with the apocalypse.

454
00:30:41.339 --> 00:30:44.591
Oh, and by the way, you suck!

